==Strategy==
It is possible to cheese the stage. Bring [[Crazy Hearts (Combo)|Crazy Hearts]], [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jellycat]] and [[Express Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bullet Train Cat]]. When the battle starts, immediately send Catellite and spam it. Right before sending your second Catellite, send Jellycat. Send these two right off cooldown for the rest of the level. Once the first Shibalien Elite gets knocked back twice, snipe him with Bullet Train Cat. Spawn Bullet Train off of cooldown as well. Once Star Peng arrives, spam [[Crazed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Mohawk Cat]] and [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cat]] as well. You may also wish to send a [[Crazed Cow Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Lion Cat]] sometime or another. If you do this correctly, you have won!

Alternatively, if you have [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] and Catellite both at level 50, you can win the stage simply by spamming them both right at the start. You can make it more consistent by bringing Starting Cash or Worker Cat [[Cat Combo|Cat Combos]].

==Trivia==
*All enemies here are [[:Category:Starred Alien Enemies|Starred Aliens]], and most have the [[Warp|warp]] ability, with the exception of [[Youcan]].
*Chapel Transfer's name may hint at how most of the stage's enemies can Warp cats, as one definition of ''transfer'' is "move from one place to another". "Chapel" may also allude to the only enemy without Warp, [[Youcan]], as chapels are places of worship and prayer and Youcan is an [[:Category:Angel Enemies|Angel]].

